    "lawCode": "Amd §2556, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1884\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to restricting the\nsale, lease, transfer or authorization of open-air schoolhouse\nplaygrounds for certain uses\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nRequires the State Education Department (SED) Commissioner to approve\nany changes or alterations to existing outdoor playground space in New\nYork City schools. The purpose of this legislation is to ensure that\nadequate outdoor playground space be provided New York City school\nchildren and that any alterations to existing playground space not be\npermitted unless an alternative plan approved by the Commissioner\nprovides space of at least equal size for outdoor recreational\nactivities.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSubdivision 5 of section 2556 requires open-air playgrounds be\nattached to all schoolhouses constructed in the city of New York. This\nlegislation amends that provision to additionally require that any\nspace leased by the City for the purposes of serving as a schoolhouse\nwill also be required to provide open-air playground space. It further\nrequires that any alterations to existing playground space which\neliminates the use of playground space for outdoor recreational\nactivities be submitted to the Commissioner for approval accompanied\nwith a plan for alternative recreational space of at least equal size\nfor outdoor recreational activities. Paragraph (a) requires plans\naltering any existing playgrounds first be submitted for approval to\nthe Commissioner. Paragraph (b) provides that such plans be reviewed\nannually by the Commissioner to ensure the need continues and that the\nplan is adequate to meet the physical education requirements for the\nstudents. Paragraph (c) provides that no alternative plan is submitted\nwithout public input from parents, teachers and community residents.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThis bill is based on the findings of a report released by Assembly\nMember Jeff Klein, as Chair of the Oversight, Analysis and\nInvestigation Committee. \"No Room In The Playground\", released in\nSeptember, 2003 found serious problems with the lack of adequate\noutdoor playground space in New York City public schools and also\nfaulted City and State education authorities for failing to ensure\nadequate outdoor playground space as the law requires. All too often\noutdoor playground space is relinquished to Temporary Classroom Units\nused to ease school overcrowding. These problems have taken on greater\nsignificance in light of the prevalence of poor health and obesity\namong today's children.\n\nCurrent law requires that alternative playground space is provided\nwhen schools built with Education Construction Funds lose this space\nto meet other school building needs. ECF constructs combined occupancy\nstructures which include certain school facilities in New York City.\nThis legislation would apply a similar provision to all school\nbuilding activities in NYC, not just those built with ECF funds.  Over\nthe years, the City has dealt with school overcrowding in a number of\nways. Sometimes the City has leased buildings to serve as additional\nschoolhouses. In the Mayor's 2005-2009 Five Year Capital Plan\n(November, 2003), 30% of the new capacity will be created by leasing\nprivate space, with capital funding proposed to make whatever\nimprovements are necessary.\n\nThis legislation ensures that whether a school is constructed or\nleased, it must provide open-air schoolhouse playgrounds and when that\nis not possible, it must provide for adequate alternatives.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2004 - A9792 - referred to education\n2006 - S2698 - referred to education\n2008 - S2239 - referred to education\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the 120th day after it shall have become\na law; provided however, that the commissioner of education is\nauthorized and directed to promulgate any rules or regulations\nnecessary for the timely implementation of this act on or before such\neffective date.\n",
